  "title": "Basque Cheesecake",
  "description": "Important tip: the batter should be mixed at low speed to avoid adding air bubbles.",
  "editorial": {
    "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Basque cheesecake is a popular recipe in Spain, where it is called 'torta de queso.' The big difference from the classic cheesecake is that it's simpler, with no crust underneath and no topping on top.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe {\"id\":26707,\"template\":\"chic-template-english\",\"updated\":1731200460368} -->\n<!--WPRM Recipe 26707-->\n<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe\">\n\t<h2 class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-name\">Basque Cheesecake</h2>\n\t<img class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-image\" src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/IMG_6106_2.Blog_-150x150.png\"/>\t<p class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-summary\">\n\t\t<p>Important tip: the batter should be mixed at low speed to avoid adding air bubbles.</p>\t</p>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-equipment\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-ingredients\">\n\t\t<ul><li>900 g softened cream cheese (such as Philadelphia)</li><li>3 pinches of salt</li><li>220 g granulated sugar</li><li>450 ml heavy cream</li><li>6 eggs</li><li>1 teaspoon liquid vanilla (or paste, or 1 vanilla pod)</li><li>30 g sifted flour</li></ul>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-instructions\">\n\t\t<ol><li><p>Preheat the oven to 190°C (thermostat 6). </p><p>Line a large pan (24 cm) with 2 layers of parchment paper.</p><br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/IMG_6081.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li><p>In a mixer bowl, beat the Philadelphia cheese at low speed with the sugar, adding the salt.</p><br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/IMG_5470.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li><p>Add the heavy cream and vanilla. Continue mixing at low speed.</p><br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/IMG_5471.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li><p>Add the eggs one by one, mixing well after each addition, still on low speed.</p><br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/IMG_5478.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li><p>Add the flour and mix once more.</p><br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/IMG_5482.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li><p>Pour the batter into the prepared pan.</p></li><li><p>Bake in the oven for about 60 minutes. The cake will rise, develop a nice golden crust, but remain slightly wobbly in the center.</p><br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/IMG_6092.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li><p>Remove the cake from the oven. Let it cool for about 2 hours, then unmold it onto a serving plate. As it cools, the cake will deflate.</p><br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/IMG_6106.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li><p>Serve at room temperature with syruped cherries or enjoy it plain.</p><br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/IMG_5521.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li></ol>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-notes\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta\">\n\t\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta-course\">Dessert</div>\t</div>\n</div>\n<!--End WPRM Recipe-->\n<!-- /wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe -->",
    "excerpt": null
  },
